                    briefing_text_r1:       `April 2026. An activist with a <strong>4.8% stake</strong> demands a credible net-zero pathway and a carbon-price step-up just added <strong>CA$90M</strong> to the 2027 bill. Before you commit a dollar, diagnose the emissions — roughly <strong>60% are process emissions</strong> inherent to making clinker, structurally hard and slow to abate, not solved by clean electricity. Then read the polarization field: ESG investors want speed, your <em>dividend base</em> fears the capex, the union has <em>480 jobs</em> at the oldest kiln, the province wants both, and NGOs are watching for greenwashing. Set an opening posture that keeps every camp at the table.`,
